.TH ARVIO 1 "2026-10-26" "arvio 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
arvio \- label eval items by hand, with the judge's answer hidden until the session ends
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arvio
[\fB\-\-no\-browser\fR]
.br
.B arvio
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGUMENT\fR ...]
.br
.B arvio \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B arvio
shows eval items to one person at a time, with the question and the meaning of each answer on screen.
The judge's answer stays hidden until the session ends.
Then arvio shows where you and the judge disagreed, and locks the labels you made.
.PP
A project talks to arvio only through files.
It writes a
.I task folder
that holds
.IR task.toml ,
.I items.jsonl
and
.IR labels.jsonl .
See
.BR arvio\-task (5)
for the format.
.PP
With no command, arvio starts the labeling page for your inbox.
The inbox is the list of task folders you added with
.BR "arvio add" .
If the inbox is empty, arvio prints how to add a task and exits with status 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-browser
With no command, print the page's link instead of opening it in a browser.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Print a short help text and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B arvio add \fR[\fB\-\-import\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR]] \fIDIR\fR
Check the task folder
.I DIR
and add it to your inbox.
Nothing is added if the check finds an error.
Adding a folder that is already in the inbox is not an error.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-import
First copy
.I task.toml
and
.I items.jsonl
into arvio's own folder,
.IR $ARVIO_DATA_DIR/tasks/NAME ,
and add that copy instead of
.IR DIR .
Labels are then written to the copy, so they no longer depend on the project's checkout.
The project's
.I labels.jsonl
is never copied.
.IP
Running the import again replaces the card and the items and keeps the labels.
It is refused, and nothing changes, if the labels would then name an item that is gone, or if a page has the folder open.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
The copy's folder name, used with
.BR \-\-import .
The default is the name of
.IR DIR .
A name has 1 to 64 characters from
.BR "a\-z 0\-9 . _ \-" ,
and starts with a letter or digit.
Using
.B \-\-name
without
.B \-\-import
is an error.
.RE
.TP
.BI "arvio remove " DIR
Take
.I DIR
off your inbox.
The folder's files stay.
Exits 1 if the folder was not in the inbox.
.TP
.BI "arvio archive " NAME_OR_DIR
Move a task to the archived list.
.I NAME_OR_DIR
is the path of a folder in your inbox, or the name of an imported task.
The folder does not move, so its labels and reports stay where they are.
A page that has the folder open is not affected.
Exits 1 if the task is not in your inbox.
.TP
.BI "arvio unarchive " NAME_OR_DIR
Move an archived task back to the active list.
.TP
.B arvio status \fR[\fB\-\-archived\fR]
For each active task in the inbox, print how many items are waiting and how many are labeled.
It also prints how many labels came from an older version of the task card, the date of the last label, and how long the next session takes.
A task that cannot be opened is listed with its first error, and the command then exits 1.
Archived tasks are left out and counted on the last line.
With
.BR \-\-archived ,
list the archived tasks instead.
.TP
.BI "arvio check " DIR
Check
.IR task.toml ,
.I items.jsonl
and
.I labels.jsonl
in
.IR DIR .
Problems go to standard error and name the file, plus the line in the two JSONL files or the setting in
.IR task.toml .
Warnings do not change the exit status.
.TP
.BI "arvio report " DIR " \fR[\fB\-\-by " META_KEY "\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]"
Compare your labels with the judge's answers.
Write
.I report.md
and
.I report.json
into
.IR DIR ,
and print the Markdown report.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-by " META_KEY"
Repeat the numbers for each value of that key in the items'
.B meta
object.
Items without the key go under
.BR (none) .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print
.I report.json
instead of the Markdown.
.RE
.IP
The report shows the count per choice and the share of "can't tell" labels.
If the task card has an
.B [agreement]
section, it also shows how many labels agree with the judge, with a 95% Wilson range,
and Cohen's kappa with a 95% range from 1,000 bootstrap resamples (seed 42, so the same labels give the same range).
.TP
.BI "arvio labels " DIR
Print the current label for each labeled item as one JSON object per line, in the order of
.IR items.jsonl .
Each line is the label row without its
.B kind
key, plus
.B "locked": true
once the judge's answers were shown for that item.
Nothing is printed if the task has an error, so a script never reads a half-checked log.
.SH THE LABELING PAGE
arvio starts a small web server for your inbox and opens the page in your browser.
Stop it with Ctrl-C.
.IP \(bu 2
The server listens only on 127.0.0.1, on a free port.
The link carries a key that changes every time arvio starts.
The server refuses API requests without the key, and requests from another host name or another page.
.IP \(bu 2
Only one arvio runs per inbox.
A task folder that another arvio holds shows as "open in another arvio" and cannot be started.
.IP \(bu 2
Items come in a fixed order made from the task card's version and the item's id.
There is no skip: "Can't tell" is the way out.
.IP \(bu 2
A choice's key picks it.
.B N
opens the note field.
.B Enter
saves and moves on.
The left arrow goes back one item.
In the inbox,
.B Enter
or
.BR 1 \- 9
opens a task.
.IP \(bu 2
The page has an Active tab and an Archived tab.
Each task has a button that moves it between them.
The page cannot start a session on an archived task until you move it back.
.IP \(bu 2
Each label is appended to
.I labels.jsonl
and synced to disk when you save it.
.IP \(bu 2
Finishing the session writes one reveal row for every item labeled under the current card that is not yet revealed, including items left from a session you closed early.
Only then does the page show the judge's answers.
Those labels are locked from then on.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
For
.BR "arvio report" ,
the report was written, and the task card's gate passed or the card has none.
.TP
.B 1
An error.
The task folder has an error, a file could not be read or written, the inbox cannot be read, or (for
.BR "arvio remove" ,
.BR "arvio archive"
and
.BR "arvio unarchive" )
the task was not in the inbox.
.BR "arvio status"
also exits 1 if any task it lists cannot be opened.
.TP
.B 2
Only from
.BR "arvio report" :
the task card sets a pass rule (a gate) and the labels do not meet it yet, including when there are too few labels.
A script can stop on this status.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ARVIO_DATA_DIR
The folder that holds the inbox and the imported tasks.
The default is
.IR ~/.arvio .
.TP
.B ARVIO_LABELER
The name written with each label.
The default is your login name.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $ARVIO_DATA_DIR/tasks.json
The inbox.
It holds the absolute paths of task folders, never items or labels.
An archived task has
.B "archived": true
in its entry.
.TP
.I $ARVIO_DATA_DIR/tasks/NAME
The copy of a task that
.B "arvio add \-\-import"
made.
.TP
.I $ARVIO_DATA_DIR/server.lock
Held by the running arvio, so only one runs per inbox.
.TP
.I DIR/task.toml
.TQ
.I DIR/items.jsonl
.TQ
.I DIR/labels.jsonl
The task folder.
See
.BR arvio\-task (5).
.TP
.I DIR/labels.jsonl.torn
Where arvio moves a last line that was cut short, before its next append.
.TP
.I DIR/report.md
.TQ
.I DIR/report.json
Written by
.BR "arvio report" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Check a task folder, add it to the inbox, and label it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
arvio check my\-task
arvio add my\-task
arvio
.fi
.RE
.PP
Keep arvio's own copy of a task, so the labels outlive the project's checkout, and later put it away:
.PP
.RS
.nf
arvio add \-\-import my\-task
arvio archive my\-task
arvio status \-\-archived
.fi
.RE
.PP
Print the link without opening a browser:
.PP
.RS
.nf
arvio \-\-no\-browser
.fi
.RE
.PP
Write the report, broken down by the items' "topic" key, and stop a script if the gate fails:
.PP
.RS
.nf
arvio report \-\-by topic my\-task || exit $?
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read the current labels in a script:
.PP
.RS
.nf
arvio labels my\-task | python3 \-c 'import json, sys; \e
print(sum(1 for line in sys.stdin if json.loads(line)["locked"]))'
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
arvio uses file locks from
.BR fcntl (2),
so it runs on macOS and Linux but not on Windows.
.PP
There is one labeler per task.
A second person's label for an item replaces the first one.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR arvio\-task (5)
.PP
The task format is also written out in
.I docs/format.md
in the arvio repository, https://github.com/jboho/arvio.
